            <ArticleTitle>[Lesions of the glenoid labrum].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>166-75</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The different lesions of the glenoid labrum are described. They may involve the antero-inferior, the posterior or the superior (SLAP lesions) part of the labrum. CT-arthrography is the gold standard imaging modality in this field of shoulder abnormalities.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
